{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794925659,"nonce":"jlYqD6RrtWiP4ii/q52QH69JQaE=","message":"68a2308 is closed, with the published window/GPU/CLI releases and green CI recorded there. Work has continued here. hxn-av's README/skill, bindings, xavi PCM/equalizer, native player and bounded codec queues were inspected first. Its AudioData conversion and native/mobile decoders remain the media path; its file player owns an output device, and its mutex-backed queues stay off the real-time render path.\n\nNew uncommitted source is in the hxn-audio sibling directory. A plain Rust core supplies overlapping voices, source resampling, bounded streams, bus routing, low-pass/delay effects and deferred resource retirement. Native output uses CPAL; browser rendering runs the same core inside an AudioWorklet over a standalone shared-memory DSP module. Ash uses its host-agent/build/serve tooling; unthreaded Emscripten dispatches on the page and does not spawn a Rust thread. The haxelib ships assets and an audio CLI namespace; its source hooks build the DSP, while installed users need no Rust or repository shell helpers. Skills and convention/design docs are being maintained with it.\n\nEvidence so far: 11 core tests and clippy pass, including repeated concurrent streaming and a render allocation/free audit; all nine functional mixer tests passed under Miri. Offline Haxe checks passed on Ash hybrid and native hxcpp/CPPIA. Actual macOS/Ash playback passed with a backend timestamp latency estimate around 11 ms. Browser playback passed on Ash and unthreaded hxcpp in Chrome, around 37 ms by WebAudio's base/output latency. The installed CLI check passed on the iOS 17.5 simulator through Ash, including pause/resume and reopening the same device, with an approximately 8 ms backend estimate. These are backend estimates, not acoustic loopback measurements. Android compilation passes; its playback/link workflow is under test. Threaded Emscripten, remaining native VM modes, hxcpp mobile, actual interruption/unplug/activation interaction, Windows/Linux CI and publication are not yet verified.\n\nA prerequisite gap was found in hxn-av: its xavi browser backend currently implements only the file player. PCM and decoder operations are not wired there. Browser output checks currently stream application PCM; they do not prove hxn-av browser decoding. Keep decoding work in hxn-av and keep this issue open until the browser decoder path and the required platform validation are complete.\n\nThe independent nullable UInt/default serialization defect found on hxcpp is tracked in c83e631ea0aee7b60ed6ae203fd2a0705db031ff9d7d91f45124f07069b1ba50. Bounded audio option counts/rates use Int with released hxn 0.3.7. No audio source commits, pushes, repository publication or git-bug push has been made.","files":null}]}